cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the released artifacts, please cite the paper below."
title: "Learning to Detect Cryptographic Defects in Ethereum Smart Contracts from Bytecode"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "[Surname]"
    given-names: "[Given Name]"
    # affiliation: "[Organization]"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Source-free detection of cryptographic defects in Ethereum smart contracts.
  A source-level analyzer is distilled into bytecode-only classifiers under a
  clone-cluster split, enabling detection on the unverified majority of on-chain
  contracts. Includes the labelled bytecode corpus splits, clone clustering,
  trained models, and the full reproduction pipeline.
keywords:
  - smart-contract security
  - cryptographic defects
  - EVM bytecode analysis
  - multi-label classification
  - knowledge distillation
